{"title":"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <i>palindrome</i> is a positive integer that is the same when read forwards or backwards. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/d/52d4135e81554e012372b44b3ccb53f4a918c9f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$545$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/6/206ca345020c7262bf8e089709eb850296aa4b93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3773$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> are both palindromes. Determine the largest five-digit palindrome whose digits have a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that the number would be formatted like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b98210049780cef6cae55804ce9c122bb1128d24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XYZYX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" /> from the description of a palindrome.\n</p><p>The largest possible number would be where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/0/d60477955db81253795e3dd972f4dae005d1be19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/f/61fd6faa4e8b9ffc9a63b3737fd0fcbe4be54770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 + 7 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, which is under <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/2/232baead1207f7962d526e6375fe2f0828d3fbc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 + 8 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> goes over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The remaining numbers must sum up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e852cad244e16079fd12c852235cddb089130d87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 - 14 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />. This would mean <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/0/86045455c73c248ce17567ca58cee5f89042d058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33cc402150215e241bfeca836abbc9c8e71a006d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/4/f04fb14b49643472fe64ba5d28c6025b0b6bf051.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2Y + Z = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />, and if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> are digits, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/e/a9efc001b4d9953bc5cb2ab93e1307214064891d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> would make the sum go over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/0/d60477955db81253795e3dd972f4dae005d1be19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33cc402150215e241bfeca836abbc9c8e71a006d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/0/86045455c73c248ce17567ca58cee5f89042d058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, the number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/9/dd928e41f96c4e56ced19ee300082d4d7a1dbd89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{70107}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"59\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC\">2025 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Pro